{#- Port of dockers/docker-fpm-frr/frr/bgpd/templates/dynamic/delete.conf.j2.

    FRR's `no neighbor NAME` removes a peer-group when NAME is one. In
    zebra-rs a neighbor and a neighbor-group are different lists, and for
    this family `neighbor_addr` is the group's name (the BGP_PEER_RANGE
    key), so it is the group that has to go. bgpcfgd removes the listen
    ranges first, in the same commit. -#}
delete router bgp neighbor-group {{ neighbor_addr }}
